Review this Go helper. The supplied writer contract says Close flushes buffered output and can return a storage error; callers must receive a failure if writing or flushing fails. The helper owns the writer.

func Save(open func() (io.WriteCloser, error), data []byte) error {
    w, err := open()
    if err != nil { return err }
    defer w.Close()
    _, err = w.Write(data)
    return err
}

Show a small correction and identify the essential checks. No atomic-replacement or crash-durability guarantee is requested.
